rkt-raft native libraries: notices

libraftrkt.so statically links the NVIDIA CUDA Runtime (libcudart_static.a,
CUDA Toolkit 13.2). The CUDA Runtime is NVIDIA's, redistributed unmodified in
object code form under the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit End User License Agreement
(https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/index.html), whose Attachment A lists it as
distributable:

    CUDA Runtime ... Linux: libcudart.so, libcudart_static.a, libcudadevrt.a

The Apache License 2.0 that covers rkt-raft does not cover the CUDA Runtime;
the Agreement's terms do, including section 1.1.2, item 2:

    The distributable portions of the SDK shall only be accessed by your
    application.

librmm.so and librapids_logger.so are RAPIDS libraries, unmodified from their
PyPI wheels, under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE.librmm,
LICENSE.rapids_logger). rkt-raft's own code is under the Apache License 2.0
(LICENSE).

